Discord Backup Linux 1.3.1

Linux-native reimplementation inspired by ItsChasa's Discord-Backup:
https://github.com/itschasa/Discord-Backup

Upstream source headers state:
Copyright (C) 2021 github.com/ItsChasa
GNU Affero General Public License v3.0

The Linux implementation uses the same documented backup concepts and legacy
JSON field names. It was implemented from inspection of the upstream README,
backup.py, restore.py, main.py and fetch_tokens.py. The upstream repository could
not be cloned in the build environment; this is a standalone reimplementation,
not a git checkout or an official upstream release. Its README labels the
repository GPL-3.0; its Python source headers specify AGPL-3.0. This distribution
uses AGPL-3.0-only consistently with those source headers.

